From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft-web, ui-egui: a finger presses the page once; a
 pinch neither selects nor takes the keyboard

Phase 6 checklist F1, F2, F6 (docs/phase6/checklist.md). On Android Chrome and WebView a finger fires `pointerdown` before `touchstart`. eframe's web runner turns both into a primary press, and its `pointerdown` handler runs a frame at once, with no touch event in it. That frame was a mouse press to the page: `touch_select` marked the last pointer a mouse (no handles, no action bar), and `canvas::mouse` placed the caret under the finger, so a press on a selection handle or on a bar button cleared the selection; the press after it (from `touchstart`) then counted as a second click (a tap selected a word). wordcraft-web now stops a finger's `pointerdown` on the canvas in the capture phase, before eframe's listener, so only `touchstart` carries a finger's press (the shape the touch code and its tests expect). A pinch: eframe presses the primary pointer again for the second finger's `touchstart`; `canvas::mouse` now leaves a press and drag during a multi-touch gesture alone, `touch_select` takes no handle press from it, and `TouchScroll` counts a pinch as a scroll so its drag does not focus the page (no soft keyboard). A mouse and a pen are unchanged.
